---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const origin = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL?.replace(/\/$/, '') || Astro.url.origin;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: origin + '/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: origin + '/privacy' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Zero-Knowledge, Zero Tracking"
  description="Media Reservoir is end-to-end encrypted and zero-knowledge: your files stay in your own storage, your keys never leave your browser, and we hold only an encrypted index. No analytics, no telemetry, no ad trackers. Read exactly what data exists and where it lives."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="legal-page">
    <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy Statement" title="Privacy Policy.">Last updated: June 20, 2026</PageHero>
    <div class="container-sm">
      <div class="legal-content">
        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Media Reservoir is designed to be <strong>zero-knowledge</strong>: your personal media belongs entirely to you, and we go out of our way to never see it. Your files are encrypted in your browser and stored in cloud storage you own; your encryption keys never leave your device. We operate a thin control plane that holds only an encrypted index — never your files, your keys, or your storage credentials in readable form.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. What We Store</h2>
          <p>
            To run your account, our servers hold a deliberately small amount of data:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account record</strong>: your email address, a hash of an authentication value derived in your browser (never your password itself), and your encrypted account-key envelopes.</li>
            <li><strong>Encrypted index</strong>: for each item, encrypted metadata such as the filename and content type, plus the storage object location. Filenames and metadata are encrypted with keys we do not have.</li>
            <li><strong>Encrypted storage settings</strong>: the configuration for the bucket you connect, encrypted in your browser before it reaches us, so your storage credentials are never readable to us.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do <strong>not</strong> store your media files (they go straight to your bucket), your password, your encryption keys, or any readable copy of your storage credentials.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>3. What We Do Not Collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>No analytics or telemetry</strong>. There are no tracking scripts, behavioral analytics, or telemetry in the application.</li>
            <li><strong>No advertising</strong>. We do not run ads or share data with advertisers or data brokers.</li>
            <li><strong>No content access</strong>. We have no technical means to read, scan, or recover your media — there is no backdoor.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            Media Reservoir uses one functional cookie:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>mv_session</code>: used strictly to authenticate your browser session. It is a cryptographic token and carries no tracking data.</li>
            <li>We do not use advertising cookies, marketing trackers, or third-party analytical cookies.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. Operational Data</h2>
          <p>
            To keep the free Service available and resistant to abuse, we apply basic rate limiting, which involves temporarily counting requests. We do not build profiles of you, and we keep operational logs to the minimum needed to run and secure the Service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. Third Parties</h2>
          <p>
            Your encrypted files are stored with the cloud storage provider <strong>you</strong> choose and connect (such as Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, Wasabi, or S3); your relationship and their handling of that data are governed by their terms and privacy policy. Our own control plane runs on Cloudflare's infrastructure. We do not sell or share your data with any other third party.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>7. Your Rights & Control</h2>
          <p>
            From your account screen you can <strong>export</strong> everything we hold for you as a single encrypted file, and <strong>delete</strong> individual items or your entire account at any time — which removes the corresponding records from our index. Because your files live in your own storage, you also retain direct and independent control over them there. Under GDPR, CCPA, and similar laws, you have rights to access, correct, and erase your data; the encrypted, minimal nature of what we hold is built to honor those rights by default.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>8. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about this policy, contact us at <a href="mailto:fantasyfalcoon91@gmail.com">fantasyfalcoon91@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .container-sm {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  .legal-page {
    padding: 0 0 96px;
  }
  .legal-page > .container-sm {
    padding-top: 60px;
  }

  .legal-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-body);
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-body);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-section a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
</style>
